# Trait Doctoring changes the words printed on a permanent, not the abilities it was given (CR 612.3; its ruling: "if you've
# changed 'green' to 'blue,' and the permanent gains protection from green ... the permanent will have protection from
# green"). Mother of Runes gives Llanowar Elves protection from red, and Trait Doctoring then replaces red with blue in the
# Elves' text: Lightning Bolt still cannot target the Elves. The positive control is the same Bolt at Mother of Runes, which has
# no protection: it is a legal target and dies. The new color may not be the old one: red is not offered to replace red.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mother of Runes
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Island
Trait Doctoring
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mother of Runes.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Trait Doctoring.Cast(Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mother of Runes.Activate(Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Colors(Red)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Replace a color word)
Bot1.Colors(Red)
! Bot1.Colors(Red)
Bot1.Colors(Blue)
Bot1.Choose()
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
! Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Mother of Runes)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Island; Llanowar Elves; Mox Pearl
Bot1.Graveyard = Mother of Runes; Trait Doctoring
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
